# Cursor rules

Full context is in CLAUDE.md. Read it before making changes; these are the rules that
matter most often.

## Architecture

- `src/core/**` is pure. No React, no `window`, no `document`. Enforced by
  `no-restricted-imports` in eslint.config.js.
- `src/dom/selection.ts` is the only module allowed to touch the DOM selection.
- Every document change goes through an operation in `core/model/operations/`.
  Nothing else builds or mutates a `Doc`.
- Operations return new objects and end with `normalizeBlock` on the blocks they
  touched. Adjacent runs with equal marks must always be merged and empty runs
  dropped, so a document has exactly one representation.
- Positions are `{ blockId, offset }` counting characters. Never a child index;
  normalization invalidates it.
- Marks are optional keys only: `{ bold: true }` or `{}`. Never `false`, never
  `undefined`.

## Style

- TypeScript strict, plus noUncheckedIndexedAccess and exactOptionalPropertyTypes.
  No `any`.
- Discriminated unions over objects with optional fields. `assertNever` in the default
  case of every switch over one.
- Tests are logic tests, run in node. No DOM snapshots. Fixtures come from
  `core/test-builders.ts`.
- Comments explain why, not what. Delete anything that restates the code.

## Before suggesting a change

- Check it against the invariants above. Most wrong answers here break one rather than
  being logically wrong.
- Include a test for the boundary case, not only the happy path.
